course: dictionary
lesson: 9271
title: Spacecraft: vehicles for space
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A spacecraft is a vehicle built to travel in space. Break the word into two parts: space and craft. A craft is a vehicle or machine, so a spacecraft is a machine for going into space. Context helps too: «Voyager 2 flew past the giant planets» tells you the vehicle is travelling far from home.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. «In 2022 the DART spacecraft bumped into an asteroid» still makes sense if you say «In 2022 the DART vehicle built to travel in space bumped into an asteroid.» Ask what it does: carry astronauts, explore planets, orbit the Earth, or send back pictures and signals.
explain: A spacecraft can be a rocket capsule, a space probe, a satellite or a space station. Some carry people, and some are robots with no one on board. In stories, a spacecraft is often called a spaceship, but in science lessons the word spacecraft is the one to use.
fact: A spacecraft is a vehicle built to travel in space.
fact: Spacecraft can carry astronauts, or travel with no people on board.
fact: «Voyager 2 is still the only spacecraft to visit Uranus and Neptune.»
fact: «Space junk» is broken satellites and pieces orbiting Earth very fast, and even a small fleck of paint can damage a spacecraft.
fact: In stories, spacecraft are often called spaceships.
exercise: «In 2022 the DART spacecraft bumped into an asteroid and changed its path.» What is a spacecraft? | A kind of fish | A computer game | *A vehicle built to travel in space | A type of rock from a planet
exercise: Which of these could be a spacecraft? | A bicycle | A rain cloud | A wooden boat | *A rocket capsule
exercise: In stories, what is a spacecraft often called? | Sailing ship | Submarine | *Spaceship | Spotlight
test: Which planets did «Voyager 2» visit that no other spacecraft has? | *Uranus and Neptune | The Moon and the Sun | Mars and Venus | Earth and Mars
test: What can a spacecraft do once it is in orbit around the Earth? | *Send back pictures and signals | Grow crops in the fields | Make rain fall | Cook a meal for astronauts
exam: Why do space agencies track space junk? | *Because even a small fleck of paint can damage a spacecraft | Because it makes a bright light in the night sky | Because it can be eaten by astronauts | Because it helps plants grow on the Moon
